  "system": {
    "role": "brute",
    "tier": 2,
    "factionId": "",
    "notes": "A hero who took a hex-pact to stay one. Plate, lance, visor down on whatever it decided to become. Keeps an oath nobody else remembers the wording of, and a toll on roads nobody gave it. The hex sings through the armor.",
    "details": {
      "level": 8,
      "tier": 2,
      "statPoints": 0,
      "skillPoints": 0,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Concept.</strong> A would-be hero who took on a hex-pact to win and is still, technically, winning. Holds a stretch of road the way a scar holds a wound.</p><p><strong>Signature.</strong> Offers single combat as a courtesy. Does not insist. Does not retreat — the oath is the road, not the people on it.</p><p><em>The old Commander Road Bandit tier-2 build (2026-10-13), knighted for the higher-tier travel tables.</em></p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
